From 34d1e6a9ad4dd4542b1adda99d615cfeee8eaf72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saikrishna Edupuganti <6157640+krsna1729@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:35:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fib6: fix table overwrite on wrap at end of address space

When a route is added or deleted, modify_dp() walks the more specific
routes it covers and moves a left edge past each one. If those routes
run contiguously up to ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff,
stepping past the last one wraps the left edge to ::. The branch taken
when the left edge is already at the next covered route does not check
for the wrap. The final range check no longer stops the walk either,
since it skips a left edge of :: (for the default route added first),
so the walk ends in install_to_dp() with both edges at ::: the next
hop is written over the whole address space. An add leaves every entry
with the added route's next hop; a delete leaves every entry with the
covering route's next hop, or the default next hop.

The common case is a change to the default route while the routes
under it reach the top of the space contiguously, such as ::/1 and
8000::/1 (as VPN clients install over a default). Adding, re-pointing
or deleting ::/0 then makes every lookup return the default route's
new next hop, or the default next hop. Any prefix ending at the last
address behaves the same: with 2001:db8::/32 -> 7 and the last two
/128 addresses -> 1 and 2, adding their /127 -> 3 makes every lookup,
2001:db8::1 included, return 3.

The commit below added the wrap check after an installed range only.
Add the same check to the branch that skips an empty range, and a test
for both cases and both operations.

Fixes: fd66617c5774 ("fib6: fix adding default route as first route")
Cc: stable@dpdk.org

[BESS: lib/ hunk only; the upstream patch also adds test_wrap_around to
app/test/test_fib6.c, made against DPDK main (its context needs the
test_drift_* cases, which 25.11.3 does not have).]

Upstream-Status: Pending
BESS-Decision: D-132
---
 lib/fib/trie.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/fib/trie.c b/lib/fib/trie.c
index 187360d1c8..59f043ce0e 100644
--- a/lib/fib/trie.c
+++ b/lib/fib/trie.c
@@ -506,6 +506,12 @@ modify_dp(struct rte_trie_tbl *dp, struct rte_rib6 *rib,
 			rte_rib6_get_ip(tmp, &redge);
 			if (rte_ipv6_addr_eq(&ledge, &redge)) {
 				get_nxt_net(&ledge, tmp_depth);
+				/*
+				 * we got to the end of address space
+				 * and wrapped around
+				 */
+				if (rte_ipv6_addr_is_unspec(&ledge))
+					break;
 				continue;
 			}
 			ret = install_to_dp(dp, &ledge, &redge, next_hop);
